# infra/php/crontab
#
# Phase 0 cron sidecar (plan §2 item 5) — runs `php cron/<job>.php` for all
# 33 jobs under cron/ on the same schedule they run on today via cPanel's
# crontab, using the same container image/code/vendor as the `php` service
# (see infra/compose/docker-compose.strangler.yml, service `cron`).
#
# *** SCHEDULES BELOW ARE INFERRED, NOT VERIFIED — REHEARSAL BLOCKER ***
# This container has no access to the production cPanel crontab, so every
# time below is inferred from the job's filename/behavior (see
# docs/ai/background-jobs.md, which itself says "Real scheduler entries
# were not inspected"). Before the real Phase 0 cutover, replace this
# entire file with the literal output of `crontab -l` on the cPanel host
# for the account that owns these jobs — see
# docs/runbooks/phase0-cutover-rollback.md item 5.
#
# /etc/cron.d format: schedule, run-as user, command. REYA_SKIP_SUBDOMAIN_RESOLUTION
# must be defined before config/database.php loads in every cron script
# (see CLAUDE.md "CLI / cron") — that's already true of every file below;
# nothing here changes that contract.
#
# Env vars available to cron jobs (cron does not inherit the container's
# shell env by default — SHELL/PATH below plus explicit `env` sourcing in
# the compose `cron` service keep DB_HOST/REDIS_*/etc. visible to PHP).
SHELL=/bin/sh
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin

# --- Broadcast jobs (docs/ai/background-jobs.md "Broadcast Jobs") ---
* * * * *      www-data    php /var/www/html/cron/send_scheduled.php >> /var/log/clinicya-cron/send_scheduled.log 2>&1
*/5 * * * *    www-data    php /var/www/html/cron/process_broadcast_queue.php >> /var/log/clinicya-cron/process_broadcast_queue.log 2>&1
